    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: 1275ca1322c2121196045179dc2244c608b0850f -->\n**Verdict: Ready for the maintainer to merge** (full review at 1275ca13; no earlier collaborator review marker existed).\n\n**What looks good**\n- `edit_tool` (crates/app/src/mcp/tool_edit.rs) runs the same undoable `ChangeTool` the GUI uses, so there is one undo step and every GUI gate applies: a retype that strands an operation, bad cutting_data, catalog values. A feeds/speeds edit has no other path.\n- Input is validated early with named errors and no unwrap/expect/panic in src: an unknown tool, a non-tool entity, a non-object patch, number/body/cutter, and unknown keys (a typed round-trip check, so a dropped edit is not reported as done).\n- New code is in `crates/app/src/mcp` and is mcp-only. The test is in `crates/app/tests` and imports `camcraft_app::mcp`. No new dependency. Provenance line is present. Files are well under 400 lines (tools.rs 312, edit.rs 288).\n- The diff against main is only the PR's 6 files; the trial merge with current main is clean, so nothing of main's was dropped. No process files, build.rs, .github or scripts are touched, so no PROCESS_VERSION bump is needed (main is at 45).\n- The body has `Changelog:` and `Fixes #1062`. The decision file `docs/decisions/1062-mcp-edit-tool.md` is present.\n\n**Local results (merged with main, own worktree)**\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test mcp_edit_tool` | 3 passed |\n| `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test recorded_post_streams` | 5 passed |\n| `cargo test -p camcraft-app --lib mcp` | no lib tests match (0 of 154) |\n| `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` | clean |\n\n**Requested before merge:** none.\n\n**Notes (not blocking)**\n1. The camcraft-mcp skill table has no `edit_tool` row yet. The PR body and decision file say so on purpose, because the skill is a process file. The law asks that a `source:agent` follow-up issue \"MCP: edit_tool skill row\" (P5, area:mcp) be named; I found no open one. Please file it and name it in the PR body.\n2. `NOT_HERE` refuses `number`; `SetToolNumber` has no MCP tool yet. This is recorded in the decision file and is fine, but it is worth a follow-up issue as well.\n\nA maintainer will approve and merge by hand.\n",
